ISO-10303-21;
HEADER;
FILE_DESCRIPTION((''),'2;1');
FILE_NAME('aggregate_paged_prefetch.ifc','2026-08-23T00:00:00',(''),(''),'','','');
FILE_SCHEMA(('IFC4'));
ENDSEC;
DATA;
/* Synthetic model for the WAVE-PAGED aggregate prefetch (conway#561 §5,
   conway#566 review).

   One IfcElementAssembly aggregating 12 IfcBuildingElementParts, each with
   its OWN representation, placement and profile — nothing shared — so every
   related product has a distinct `#ref` closure and "how much of the
   relationship has been paged" is observable by counting records.

   RelatedObjects also holds four non-products, none of which is an
   IfcProduct, so the aggregates pass materialises each (from the columns —
   it reads no source bytes to decide) and walks past it without extracting
   or yielding. See extractRelAggregateGeometryIncremental's
   `instanceof IfcProduct` guard.

     #150            one IfcGroup, mid-list
     #160 #161 #170  a RUN of three, between two parts
     #151            one IfcGroup, after the last part

   The run is what makes `waveSize` a bound rather than a suggestion: a
   prefetch that paged related-object ENTRIES rather than related PRODUCTS
   would have to span the whole run to reach the next product, whatever its
   wave size. #170 is an IfcFurnitureType carrying RepresentationMaps into a
   398-face IfcFacetedBrep — 1,607 records of closure on its own, measured —
   so a prefetch that pages it is obvious in the pin counts. Nothing reads
   those bytes: only extractProductGeometry reads a record, and it runs for
   products only.

   The trailing #151 is past the last yield entirely, so no later step
   exists for a wave to be carried by.

   The non-products are declared in the MIDDLE of the part records,
   deliberately: a test behind a narrow window can only tell "paged" from
   "not paged" for a record whose bytes nothing else pins, and the
   relationship's own record (last) and the assembly's (first) pin the two
   ends of the file for the relationship's whole life. */
#1=IFCPROJECT('CxLS067y1lcJywHUOaW903',$,'AggregatePagedPrefetch',$,$,$,$,(#20),#10);
#10=IFCUNITASSIGNMENT((#11));
#11=IFCSIUNIT(*,.LENGTHUNIT.,$,.METRE.);
